# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Zhanghao Zhouyin et al. (2024). Learning local equivariant representations for quantum operators.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2407.06053  arXiv:2407.06053v4
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2407.06053v4 (sha256 99f0ead45d4e9fc1...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 86 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: bibliographic facts only. SLEM is a strictly local
# equivariant message-passing model that predicts quantum operators in a
# local-orbital basis (Kohn-Sham Hamiltonian, density matrix, overlap
# matrix). It is not an interatomic potential: it predicts no energies or
# forces as a function of atomic positions for use in atomistic
# simulation.

